menu "Roottask"

config ROOTTASK_HEAP_SIZE
    int "Roottask malloc heap size (bytes)"
    default 524288
    range 131072 16777216
    help
      Size of the fixed arena that backs roottask's malloc. Roottask is the
      mmap server, so unlike every other process it cannot grow its heap
      by mapping memory. Must be a multiple of 4096.

      Default: 524288 (512 KiB).

config ROOTTASK_SYSLOG_SIZE
    int "Roottask log buffer size (bytes)"
    default 1048576
    help
      Size of the roottask ring buffer for diagnostic messages.
      All root_log/root_dbg/root_trace output is stored here and can
      be read as /sys/log (mode 0400, root only).

      Default: 1048576 (1 MiB).

config ROOTTASK_SYSLOG_STDOUT
    bool "Echo roottask log to console"
    default y
    help
      When enabled, roottask log messages are also printed to the
      system console via kprintf.  Debug and trace messages are
      filtered by the kernel's loglevel (-v / -vv).

      Disable this to suppress all roottask console output and
      rely solely on the ring buffer.

endmenu
